course: dictionary
lesson: 8700
title: Semantic: all about meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Semantic is a long word with a simple job: it means to do with the meanings of words and sentences. When you ask what a word really means, you are asking a semantic question. «When a word's meaning changes over time, it is called semantic change.» Here semantic tells you that the change is in meaning, not in spelling or sound.
explain: Semantics is the study of meaning in language. It is a noun that takes a singular verb, so we say «Semantics is interesting», not «Semantics are interesting». Writers and readers use it to think about why one word fits a sentence and another does not.
explain: Sometimes people say «That is just semantics» when they argue about which word to use, not about the real facts. If one friend says a rock pool is small and another says it is tiny, they may agree on the facts, so the argument is just semantics.
fact: Semantic means to do with the meanings of words and sentences.
fact: Semantics is the study of meaning in language.
fact: «Semantic change» means a word's meaning changes over time.
fact: A semantic field is a group of words about one topic, such as war: battle, soldier, attack.
fact: In computing, «semantic search» finds results by meaning rather than exact words.
exercise: «When a word's meaning changes over time, it is called semantic change.» What does semantic mean here? | *To do with meaning | To do with size | To do with sound | To do with spelling
exercise: Which word is the noun for the study of meaning in language? | *semantics | meaningful | semantic
exercise: Battle, soldier and attack are words about war. What is this group of words called? | Semantic change | *A semantic field | A semantic search
test: What does «That is just semantics» mean? | We are arguing about the weather | *We are arguing about words, not facts | We are arguing about the facts | Nobody is arguing
test: Which sentence uses semantics correctly? | Semantics be interesting | Semantics are interesting | *Semantics is interesting
exam: In computing, what does «semantic search» find results by? | The colour of the words | *Meaning rather than exact words | Exact words only | The length of the words
